    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d324">

                <pb facs="0263" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/247</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nagasaki</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-20T10:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 20,
                                1917, 10 a.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 12.16 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Willard:</p>
                <p>Again strongly advise holding units in Japan. I ought to know shortly if we can
                    go ahead. All units must take some food and bedding on their return to Russia;
                    therefore, both Emerson and Baldwin must
                    be supplied ample funds. We should all go back <pb facs="0264" n="214"
                        xml:id="pg214"/> shortly with man-of-war and 5,000 troops. Time is coming to
                    put fear of God into these people. Answer care of Consul of the United States,
                    Yokohama.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
